{
  "configuration_id": "config_015",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_033 (pca_n2000, resnet50, avgpool, concat) is the best result at 0.6186 acc, showing that multimodal fusion over RNA-only (0.5907) provides a modest gain, and that avgpool aggregation outperforms transformer (config_014, 0.5793). However, all multimodal results so far use concat fusion; we have no data on whether weighted fusion could further improve performance. Question: config_015 changes only the fusion method (concat → weighted) while holding every other variable at its best-known value (pca_n2000, resnet50, avgpool, multiprofile). This isolates the effect of the fusion mechanism. Why this is the best next experiment: it is a clean single-variable comparison to config_033, directly testing an important and currently unexplored design axis (fusion strategy). If weighted fusion helps, it identifies a clear improvement path; if not, it confirms concat is sufficient and redirects budget toward other axes (e.g., image encoder or RNA encoder). This is more informative than testing imagenet_vit_l (image-only results show resnet50 and vit_l are nearly identical at ~0.33, suggesting low expected information gain in the multimodal context) or scvi_n200 (pca_n2000 already strongly outperforms scgpt, making scvi_n200 less likely to change the picture)."
}

